saints row is a series that is bursting  with secrets developer volition has  hidden little details and easter eggs  throughout each of the mainline titles  in this bombastic selection of games to  entice the player into the great unknown  or more likely just some dungeon some of  these are in-game some are tidbits  surrounding the greater development of  the series itself but these are 10  things you didn't know about saints row  number 10  chuck nick's books throughout the city  of stillwater in the first saints row  you will come across buildings labeled  chuck nicks books this is a reference to  chuck palahniuk the writer of the  invention of sound and most famously  fight club and always remember the first  rule of fight club is to have fun and be  yourself  number nine  the merman  in saints row two if you head to the  eastern side of the hotels and marina  district scrawled on a billboard is the  warning beware the merman along with a  small note describing the creature as  flippered and dangerous  the note also explains that the being  has been sighted off the shores of the  marina a random npc even references the  creature saying legend has it there's a  half man half fish who lives down here  although the painted monster depicts a  half-man half-shark-like hybrid the real  merman turns out to be brian murman a  member of the saints row 2 art team  number eight missing ships in saints row  the third if you enter any of the cargo  ships in game you'll find a list of  missing ships these range from real-life  disappearances to fictional ships the  developers love the list goes as follows  the bachemo this is a reference to the  uss bachmo a real-life ghost ship that  supposedly was abandoned off the coast  of alaska in 1931. it was cited multiple  times for decades after its abandonment  with its last sighting in 1969 hms  seahorse i couldn't find any information  on ships named the hms seahorse that  were lost at sea further adding to the  mystery of its addition to this list the  axiom this is the fictional spacecraft  that the entire population of earth  lives on in the disney pixar film wally  the usg ishimura another fictional  spacecraft this time the zombie alien  infested spaceship from the dead space  series of games the octavius this is a  real-life legendary ship found off the  coast of greenland in which the entire  crew froze to death and were perfectly  preserved as the story goes the captain  was frozen stiff at his desk with a  quill in hand writing his captain's log  the borealis this is the fictional but  pivotal resistance vessel in the  half-life series appearing in both  episodes of half-life 2 as well as an  eluded cameo in portal 2 the heart of  gold  this is the fictional spacecraft from  the hitchhiker's guide to the galaxy  series the mary's celeste a real-life  ship that was completely abandoned with  no trace of the crew it was later  immortalized by many retellings  including a famous fictional retelling  by sir arthur conan doyle the uss snook  this is a real-life u.s navy submarine  that was lost without a trace near the  philippines in 1945.  number seven the red faction series  there's a lot of cross-referencing and  potential universe combining between the  saints row series and red faction series  volition developer of both series has  denied any connection between the two  just some heartfelt homages and winks  towards each other the most major  connective tissue between the two games  is the altor corporation throughout  saints row and saints row 2 the altor  corporation rose from a smaller company  that sponsored sports teams in saints  row to a mega corporation and main  antagonist in saints row 2. they  seemingly continued their evil doings  from earth to mars where they were the  main antagonist in the first red faction  game smaller but fun tidbits that pull  the worlds together are red planet red  passion and red fiction used books in  saints row 2 a radio ad advertises the  tv show red planet red passion a drama  about a mining colony on mars two of the  characters in the show are parker and  eos both characters featured in red  faction red fiction used books is a used  bookstore in the summerset district in  saints row in saints row 2 that shares  the same logo and naming convention as  red faction one of the last major  connections between the two series comes  in the gangstas in space mission in  saints row the third in the final cut  scene your character will start to  recite a speech and then forget his line  this speech is word for word the same as  the one main character alec mason gives  at the end of red faction gorilla to  further the link if you chose the male 1  voice when creating your character the  lines will be said by voice actor troy  baker  voice of alex mason  and some other stuff  nothing big  [Music]  number six pc project red before  becoming the powerhouse behind the  witcher series cd project red just known  as cd project in 2009 was tasked by thq  to make a port of saints row 2 for the  pc according to numerous reports the  port was a buggy mess on release and due  to thq auctioning off all of its assets  after going bankrupt in 2013 the source  code of the pc version was thought to be  completely lost after years of being  almost unplayable in 2019 volitions  stated that they had found the source  code and began patching the game with  steam and mod support  number five the 31 theory before i begin  this theory i want to talk about the  trope of arc numbers have you ever been  watching or reading something and a  certain number comes up again and again  that makes you go  these  are arc numbers  arc numbers are numbers in a fictional  work that pop up again and again with no  contextual connection in saints row the  magic number is 31 or it's inverse 13.  and this is not a theory i've made up in  my mind like some over-caffeinated  theorists in saints row the third during  a homie conversation kinsey relates the  thirty-one theory the thirty-one theory  anything important is always connected  to a thirty-one nightblade season three  best season aired in january had 13  episodes  season 3 aired on the first month of the  year 13 episodes  31-13  and although this theory is stated for  the first time in the third game in the  series the 31 chambers have appeared in  every game the list is long and i'm not  going to read all of the references  but i'll read some as fast as possible  saints row the king penthouse code is  3131 there are 31 discrete items in the  funky fresh pack there are 31  single-player achievements and 31 wins  to achieve the true skill rank for  kingpin saints row 2. there's a mission  called assaults on precinct 31 which is  also a reference to the movie assault on  precinct 13. gap mentions his jail time  was 2 years and 31 days the news channel  in game is news 13 stillwater one hitman  mission has you tracking down an  arsonist that has burned down 31  buildings there are 31 taunts and  compliments for your gang saints row the  third one level is called 31 days later  referencing 28 days later murder brawl  31 occurs during the course of the game  the clapper at the end of the gangstas  and space mission says that you are on  take 31 and on a saints row website  profile in real life johnny gatt's  birthday is labeled as 1980 with his  death in 2011 making him you guessed it  31 saints row 4. a new code 1331 comes  up in the mission platforming rift  kinsey who created this theory in game  states that her planetary defense budget  is 3.1 million dollars zinyak refers to  you as special prisoner 31 and when  choosing a character from the  customization presets choosing option 6  mentions the 31st amendment so there you  go  volition loves that good old lucky  thirty one  [Music]  number four saints row two secret areas  as stated at the beginning of this video  saints row is a series that is bursting  with secrets  this is no more apparent than in sain